":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Senate Appropriations Subcommittee on Homeland Security hearing 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Subcommittee Hearing\",\"url\":\"https://www.appropriations.senate.gov/hearings/a-review-of-the-presidents-fiscal-year-2027-budget-request-for-the-department-of-homeland-security\"},{\"title\":\"U.S. Senator Katie Britt Chairs Homeland Security Appropriations Subcommittee Hearing on FY26 DHS Budget Proposal\",\"url\":\"https://www.britt.senate.gov/news/press-releases/u-s-senator-katie-britt-chairs-homeland-security-appropriations-subcommittee-hearing-on-fy26-dhs-budget-proposal\"},{\"title\":\"search.law.villanova.edu\",\"url\":\"https://search.law.villanova.edu/Record/415906\"},{\"title\":\"Subcommittee Hearing\",\"url\":\"https://www.appropriations.senate.gov/hearings/a-review-of-the-presidents-fiscal-year-2026-budget-request-for-the-department-of-homeland-security\"},{\"title\":\"owt guidelines homeland fy 26&download=1\",\"url\":\"https://www.appropriations.senate.gov/download/owt-guidelines-homeland-fy-26&download=1\"},{\"title\":\"WATCH LIVE: Kristi Noem testifies at Senate Appropriations Committee\",\"url\":\"https://www.denvergazette.com/?p=377304\"},{\"title\":\"homeland security appropriations\",\"url\":\"https://fedbudgetguy.substack.com/p/homeland-security-appropriations\"},{\"title\":\"homeland security member day 0\",\"url\":\"https://appropriations.house.gov/schedule/hearings/homeland-security-member-day-0\"},{\"title\":\"search.law.villanova.edu\",\"url\":\"https://search.law.villanova.edu/Record/410168/Channels\"},{\"title\":\"ed84ce83 1306 4bfe 957c 9663f9c8a47a\",\"url\":\"https://capitolreleases.com/releases/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\"}]\n\nThe most relevant 2026 result is a Senate Appropriations Subcommittee on Homeland Security hearing on the fiscal year 2027 budget request, held Tuesday, June 2, 2026, in Dirksen 138. Chair Katie Britt presided, and the witnesses listed were Deputy Secretary Troy Edgar and Secretary Markwayne Mullin of the Department of Homeland Security.\n\nOther results are older or less specific:\n\n- **FY2026 DHS budget hearing (May 2025):** Britt's subcommittee questioned then-Secretary Kristi Noem on the FY26 request. That hearing was held Thursday, May 8, 2025, at 10:00 AM in Dirksen 124.\n- **FY2026 Senate bill:** A fedbudgetguy tracker says Senate Appropriations Republicans released the Homeland Security bill on 12/19/25 without bipartisan agreement.\n- **Written testimony for FY26:** The subcommittee had not scheduled any outside witness hearings on FY2026 appropriations, though written testimony was still accepted.\n\nI did not find a full list of other 2026 subcommittee hearings, so the FY2027 hearing above is the only confirmed 2026 event in these results. The Senate Appropriations Committee's hearings page would be the best place to check for others.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","uuid":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","timestamp":"2026-10-24T00:35:53.398Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Senate Appropriations Subcommittee on Homeland Security hearing 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_000000","content":[{"title":"Subcommittee Hearing","url":"https://www.appropriations.senate.gov/hearings/a-review-of-the-presidents-fiscal-year-2027-budget-request-for-the-department-of-homeland-security"},{"title":"U.S. Senator Katie Britt Chairs Homeland Security Appropriations Subcommittee Hearing on FY26 DHS Budget Proposal","url":"https://www.britt.senate.gov/news/press-releases/u-s-senator-katie-britt-chairs-homeland-security-appropriations-subcommittee-hearing-on-fy26-dhs-budget-proposal"},{"title":"search.law.villanova.edu","url":"https://search.law.villanova.edu/Record/415906"},{"title":"Subcommittee Hearing","url":"https://www.appropriations.senate.gov/hearings/a-review-of-the-presidents-fiscal-year-2026-budget-request-for-the-department-of-homeland-security"},{"title":"owt guidelines homeland fy 26&download=1","url":"https://www.appropriations.senate.gov/download/owt-guidelines-homeland-fy-26&download=1"},{"title":"WATCH LIVE: Kristi Noem testifies at Senate Appropriations Committee","url":"https://www.denvergazette.com/?p=377304"},{"title":"homeland security appropriations","url":"https://fedbudgetguy.substack.com/p/homeland-security-appropriations"},{"title":"homeland security member day 0","url":"https://appropriations.house.gov/schedule/hearings/homeland-security-member-day-0"},{"title":"search.law.villanova.edu","url":"https://search.law.villanova.edu/Record/410168/Channels"},{"title":"ed84ce83 1306 4bfe 957c 9663f9c8a47a","url":"https://capitolreleases.com/releases/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"}]},"The most relevant 2026 result is a Senate Appropriations Subcommittee on Homeland Security hearing on the fiscal year 2027 budget request, held Tuesday, June 2, 2026, in Dirksen 138. Chair Katie Britt presided, and the witnesses listed were Deputy Secretary Troy Edgar and Secretary Markwayne Mullin of the Department of Homeland Security.\n\nOther results are older or less specific:\n\n- **FY2026 DHS budget hearing (May 2025):** Britt's subcommittee questioned then-Secretary Kristi Noem on the FY26 request. That hearing was held Thursday, May 8, 2025, at 10:00 AM in Dirksen 124.\n- **FY2026 Senate bill:** A fedbudgetguy tracker says Senate Appropriations Republicans released the Homeland Security bill on 12/19/25 without bipartisan agreement.\n- **Written testimony for FY26:** The subcommittee had not scheduled any outside witness hearings on FY2026 appropriations, though written testimony was still accepted.\n\nI did not find a full list of other 2026 subcommittee hearings, so the FY2027 hearing above is the only confirmed 2026 event in these results. The Senate Appropriations Committee's hearings page would be the best place to check for others."],"durationSeconds":5.7649607419999995,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_000000","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reason_type":"rule"}}]},{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_000000","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Senate Appropriations Committee Homeland Security subcommittee jurisdiction ICE detention funding\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"dhs fy22 funding letter\",\"url\":\"https://www.warren.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/dhs_fy22_funding_letter.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"assets.aila.org\",\"url\":\"https://assets.aila.org/files/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/18051633.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"chairwoman roybal allard statement at subcommittee markup of fy 2021 homeland\",\"url\":\"https://democrats-appropriations.house.gov/news/statements/chairwoman-roybal-allard-statement-at-subcommittee-markup-of-fy-2021-homeland\"},{\"title\":\"stop enabling ices dangerous detention and reckless deportation drive oppose additional funding in the fy2026 homeland security appropriations bill\",\"url\":\"https://humanrightsfirst.org/library/stop-enabling-ices-dangerous-detention-and-reckless-deportation-drive-oppose-additional-funding-in-the-fy2026-homeland-security-appropriations-bill/\"},{\"title\":\"Prepping to Spend More for Migrant Detention: Starting Line\",\"url\":\"https://news.bgov.com/bloomberg-government-news/congress-prepares-to-spend-more-on-ice-detention\"},{\"title\":\"johnjoyce.house.gov\",\"url\":\"https://johnjoyce.house.gov/sites/evo-subsites/johnjoyce.house.gov/files/evo-media-document/FY25%20Homeland%20Consolidated%20Letter%202.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Senate Spending Bill Continues Misguided Enforcement Approach\",\"url\":\"https://immigrantjustice.org/press-release/senate-spending-bill-continues-misguided-enforcement-approach/\"},{\"title\":\"aila.org\",\"url\":\"https://aila.org/aila-files/E7F69733-803E-4D1E-96AB-2AF049FCE83F/17062235.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"HomelandLetter Frelinghuysen\",\"url\":\"https://trumpwhitehouse.archives.gov/wp-content/uploads/2018/07/HomelandLetter-Frelinghuysen.pdf\"}]\n\nThe search returned mostly older material, and nothing that confirms the current Senate subcommittee leadership or jurisdiction.\n\n- **Structure:** Senate DHS spending runs through the Appropriations Committee's Homeland Security subcommittee. Letters from 2017, 2018, and 2021 are addressed to that subcommittee's chair and ranking member, and they lobby on detention and enforcement levels. The 2021 letter is addressed to the full committee chair and the subcommittee chair, with the vice chair and ranking member also named.\n- **Detention funding history:** A 2021 House subcommittee statement notes that the bill funded an average daily population in ICE custody of 22,000 single adults. A 2024 advocacy letter says detention bed capacity under ICE was a priority request for the FY2025 bill.\n- **Recent bills:** An advocacy group opposing the FY2026 homeland security bill said Congress reportedly was nearing an agreement to fund DHS for 44,500 immigration detention beds. It also noted that this was up from 41,500 beds appropriated for FY24, on top of funds from the 2025 reconciliation law. That source is an advocacy piece, so treat its figures as contested.\n- **Caveat:** The most recent items are advocacy statements and a 2025 Bloomberg Government piece about the House draft. I found no official Senate Appropriations text, current subcommittee chair, or FY2027 status. A follow-up search on the Senate Appropriations Committee's own site for the current FY2027 DHS bill would be needed to confirm those.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","uuid":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","timestamp":"2026-10-24T00:35:54.243Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Senate Appropriations Committee Homeland Security subcommittee jurisdiction ICE detention funding","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_000000","content":[{"title":"dhs fy22 funding letter","url":"https://www.warren.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/dhs_fy22_funding_letter.pdf"},{"title":"assets.aila.org","url":"https://assets.aila.org/files/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/18051633.pdf"},{"title":"chairwoman roybal allard statement at subcommittee markup of fy 2021 homeland","url":"https://democrats-appropriations.house.gov/news/statements/chairwoman-roybal-allard-statement-at-subcommittee-markup-of-fy-2021-homeland"},{"title":"stop enabling ices dangerous detention and reckless deportation drive oppose additional funding in the fy2026 homeland security appropriations bill","url":"https://humanrightsfirst.org/library/stop-enabling-ices-dangerous-detention-and-reckless-deportation-drive-oppose-additional-funding-in-the-fy2026-homeland-security-appropriations-bill/"},{"title":"Prepping to Spend More for Migrant Detention: Starting Line","url":"https://news.bgov.com/bloomberg-government-news/congress-prepares-to-spend-more-on-ice-detention"},{"title":"johnjoyce.house.gov","url":"https://johnjoyce.house.gov/sites/evo-subsites/johnjoyce.house.gov/files/evo-media-document/FY25%20Homeland%20Consolidated%20Letter%202.pdf"},{"title":"Senate Spending Bill Continues Misguided Enforcement Approach","url":"https://immigrantjustice.org/press-release/senate-spending-bill-continues-misguided-enforcement-approach/"},{"title":"aila.org","url":"https://aila.org/aila-files/E7F69733-803E-4D1E-96AB-2AF049FCE83F/17062235.pdf"},{"title":"HomelandLetter Frelinghuysen","url":"https://trumpwhitehouse.archives.gov/wp-content/uploads/2018/07/HomelandLetter-Frelinghuysen.pdf"}]},"The search returned mostly older material, and nothing that confirms the current Senate subcommittee leadership or jurisdiction.\n\n- **Structure:** Senate DHS spending runs through the Appropriations Committee's Homeland Security subcommittee. Letters from 2017, 2018, and 2021 are addressed to that subcommittee's chair and ranking member, and they lobby on detention and enforcement levels. The 2021 letter is addressed to the full committee chair and the subcommittee chair, with the vice chair and ranking member also named.\n- **Detention funding history:** A 2021 House subcommittee statement notes that the bill funded an average daily population in ICE custody of 22,000 single adults. A 2024 advocacy letter says detention bed capacity under ICE was a priority request for the FY2025 bill.\n- **Recent bills:** An advocacy group opposing the FY2026 homeland security bill said Congress reportedly was nearing an agreement to fund DHS for 44,500 immigration detention beds. It also noted that this was up from 41,500 beds appropriated for FY24, on top of funds from the 2025 reconciliation law. That source is an advocacy piece, so treat its figures as contested.\n- **Caveat:** The most recent items are advocacy statements and a 2025 Bloomberg Government piece about the House draft. I found no official Senate Appropriations text, current subcommittee chair, or FY2027 status. A follow-up search on the Senate Appropriations Committee's own site for the current FY2027 DHS bill would be needed to confirm those."],"durationSeconds":6.412842683000001,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_000000","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reason_type":"rule"}}]},{"type":"system","subtype":"thinking_tokens","estimated_tokens":50,"estimated_tokens_delta":50,"session_id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","uuid":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"},{"type":"system","subtype":"thinking_tokens","estimated_tokens":300,"estimated_tokens_delta":250,"session_id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","uuid":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"},{"type":"system","subtype":"thinking_tokens","estimated_tokens":550,"estimated_tokens_delta":250,"session_id":"0000